{{smaller block|<poem>He that shall live this day, and see old age,
Will yearly on the ''vigil'' feast his neighbours,
And say, “To-morrow is St. Crispian.”</poem>
{{right|''Shak.'', Hen. V., iv. 3. 45.}}}}
